Compensation Available Under California Lemon Law

Successful Lemon Law claims may result in several forms of compensation. California law aims to place consumers in a fair financial position after repeated warranty failures. Possible outcomes include:

- Vehicle buyback reimbursement

- Replacement vehicle options

- Reimbursement for repair expenses

- Coverage of attorney fees and court costs

- Payment for related incidental expenses

Manufacturers may become responsible for attorney fees when consumers prevail under California Lemon Law statutes. This structure allows many drivers to pursue claims without large upfront legal expenses.

Buyback Calculations

Vehicle buyback amounts often include:

- Down payment amounts

- Monthly payments

- Registration fees

- Taxes

- Certain out-of-pocket expenses

Mileage deductions may apply depending on when the defect first appeared.

